      "problem": "What number is $155%$ greater than $40?$",
      "worked_solution": "To find a number $155%$ *greater than* $40,$ we apply a new percentage of\n\n$$\n100%+155%=255%.\n$$\n\nWe begin by converting the percentage to a decimal:\n\n$$\n255%=\\frac{255}{100}=2.55\n$$\n\nSo, to find a number that is $155%$ greater than $40,$ we multiply $40$ by $2.55:$\n\n$$\n2.55\\cdot 40=102\n$$\n\nTherefore, the number that is $155%$ greater than $40$ is $102.$",
